# Upstream Notes

> Living record of upstream PRs filed (or pending) against
> [github/spec-kit](https://github.com/github/spec-kit) by this fork.
> Constitution P1 (NON-NEGOTIABLE) requires that any divergence from
> upstream's `src/specify_cli/` be filed as an upstream PR and tracked
> here — local patches are forbidden.

Upstream baseline: **v0.8.10** — commit `0e5b59fcaa1deb976c1f73b47c743de1cf5a5d71`.

---

## T048 — `specify init --preset linear --extension linear` verification

**Date verified**: 2026-05-15
**Branch**: `upstream-sync-0.8.10`
**Outcome**: The full Contract C1 surface is **not yet present in upstream
v0.8.10**. Smoke run on a freshly built venv:

```text
$ specify init --ignore-agent-tools --integration claude \
               --preset linear --extension linear --no-git /tmp/proj
Error: No such option: --extension
```

`--preset linear` *alone* succeeds and installs the bundled
`presets/linear/` correctly — the gap is the new flag surface required
by [PMO-76 Contract C1](https://linear.app/pmo-to-do-list/issue/PMO-76),
not the preset itself.

### Upstream gaps to land via PR

1. **`--extension <name>` flag** (repeatable). Mirrors `--preset` and
   lets `specify init` install one or more extensions in the same call.
2. **`--preset` becomes repeatable** (list[str] not str).
3. **Preset↔extension pairing check**: `--preset linear` without
   `--extension linear` exits 4 with the documented message
   (PMO-76 §C1 — "Behavior contract — Linear pairing").
4. **MCP pre-flight**: when a preset/extension declares a required MCP
   tool, attempt one read call before mutating the workspace; on
   failure exit 3 with the `claude mcp add …` hint.
5. **Exit-code remap**: directory conflict currently exits 1; Contract
   C1 specifies exit 5. Either remap upstream or accept the divergence
   in the contract document.
6. **`--dry-run`, `-v/-vv`, `--all-agents`, `--target <path>` flags** —
   see PMO-76 §C1 for the full schema.

### Tracking

* Contract test: `tests/cli/test_init_contract.py` (T047) — every
  assertion above is encoded as an `xfail(strict=False)` and will flip
  to green automatically once upstream merges.
* Upstream PR: **TODO — open against `github/spec-kit` main once the
  Phase 4 vendor refresh stabilises.** Link will be added here.
* Until upstream merges, the Linear extension's `before_specify` hook
  performs the pairing and MCP pre-flight checks locally (no patch to
  `src/specify_cli/` — the validation lives behind the extension API).

### Workaround for end users today

```bash
# Works today against upstream v0.8.10 with this fork's bundled preset:
specify init --ai claude --preset linear --here
# Then in the new project, install the linear extension:
specify extension install linear
```

Once the upstream PR lands, the documented one-shot form will work:

```bash
specify init --ai claude --preset linear --extension linear --here
```
